From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos990: give the Bluetooth UART its RTS pin

The stock DT (`uart@10840000`) puts all four pins gpq0-0..3 on the UART
function. The port uses `uart1_bus_norts`, so the host cannot throttle the
QCA6390; hci_qca enables flow control and at 3 Mbit/s the 256 B RX FIFO
fills in ~0.85 ms. Dropped bytes break H4 framing, matching the
"desynchronises after hundreds of segments" symptom
(research/wifi-bt-firmware.md). Use `uart1_bus_single` (4 pins) as stock.

Untested on the device.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos990.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos990.dtsi
@@ -913,7 +913,7 @@
 				clock-names = "uart", "clk_uart_baud0";
 				samsung,uart-fifosize = <256>;
 				pinctrl-names = "default";
-				pinctrl-0 = <&uart1_bus_norts>;
+				pinctrl-0 = <&uart1_bus_single>;
 				status = "okay";
 
 				bluetooth {
